1
00:00:00,700 --> 00:00:03,985
In the Ethiopian Bible,
there is a prison for stars.

2
00:00:04,435 --> 00:00:07,931
Seven stars, burning like
great mountains, bound in a

3
00:00:07,931 --> 00:00:10,899
place with no sky above
and no earth beneath.

4
00:00:11,349 --> 00:00:14,571
Their crime? They did not rise
at their appointed times.

5
00:00:15,021 --> 00:00:17,917
An angel showed this to
a man named Enoch. And

6
00:00:17,917 --> 00:00:20,183
it was only one stop on his journey.

7
00:00:20,633 --> 00:00:22,809
What else did he see at
the ends of the earth?

8
00:00:24,759 --> 00:00:28,322
Last time, Enoch carried a
message to the fallen Watchers.

9
00:00:28,772 --> 00:00:32,142
Then angels like flaming
fire took him on a journey:

10
00:00:32,142 --> 00:00:35,641
chapters seventeen to thirty‑six
of the Book of Enoch.

11
00:00:36,091 --> 00:00:39,048
The whole book survives
only in Ge'ez, kept by

12
00:00:39,048 --> 00:00:41,233
the Ethiopian Church as scripture.

13
00:00:41,683 --> 00:00:45,188
These chapters are over two
thousand years old. Pieces of

14
00:00:45,188 --> 00:00:47,955
them in Aramaic were
found near the Dead Sea.

15
00:00:48,405 --> 00:00:50,559
So where did the angels take him first?

16
00:00:52,509 --> 00:00:55,432
To a mountain whose summit
reached to heaven, and

17
00:00:55,432 --> 00:00:57,757
a river of fire that flowed like water.

18
00:00:58,207 --> 00:01:00,365
He saw the storehouses of the winds, and

19
00:01:00,365 --> 00:01:01,983
the corner‑stone of the earth.

20
00:01:02,433 --> 00:01:06,323
Seven mountains of precious
stones. The middle one like the

21
00:01:06,323 --> 00:01:09,751
throne of God: alabaster,
with a summit of sapphire.

22
00:01:10,201 --> 00:01:13,337
And Enoch wrote: no man
shall see as I have seen.

23
00:01:13,787 --> 00:01:17,264
But the strangest place was still
ahead. Where do the dead wait?

24
00:01:19,214 --> 00:01:22,024
In the west stood a high
mountain of hard rock,

25
00:01:22,024 --> 00:01:24,057
with four hollow places inside it.

26
00:01:24,507 --> 00:01:27,651
The angel Raphael explained:
here the souls of the

27
00:01:27,651 --> 00:01:30,544
dead are gathered, until
the day of judgement.

28
00:01:30,994 --> 00:01:33,808
In the Greek copy, three
are dark. One is bright,

29
00:01:33,808 --> 00:01:36,221
with a spring of water, for the righteous.

30
00:01:36,671 --> 00:01:39,849
And from one hollow, a voice
was crying out to heaven.

31
00:01:40,299 --> 00:01:43,521
It was Abel, still pleading against
the brother who killed him.

32
00:01:45,471 --> 00:01:47,996
Did you know? Scholars
call this the earliest

33
00:01:47,996 --> 00:01:50,185
Jewish description of life after death.

34
00:01:50,635 --> 00:01:53,600
Compare the parable in
Luke sixteen: between the

35
00:01:53,600 --> 00:01:56,502
righteous and the rich
man, a great gulf fixed.

36
00:01:56,952 --> 00:01:59,528
And what did Enoch do,
after seeing the dead?

37
00:01:59,528 --> 00:02:01,645
He blessed the Lord of righteousness.

38
00:02:03,595 --> 00:02:07,359
Then he came to seven magnificent
mountains. The seventh

39
00:02:07,359 --> 00:02:10,315
was like a throne, ringed
by fragrant trees.

40
00:02:10,765 --> 00:02:13,622
Among them stood a tree
with a fragrance beyond

41
00:02:13,622 --> 00:02:15,992
all fragrance. Its leaves never wither.

42
00:02:16,442 --> 00:02:18,951
The archangel Michael said: no mortal may

43
00:02:18,951 --> 00:02:21,093
touch it until the great judgement.

44
00:02:21,543 --> 00:02:24,031
Then its fruit will feed
the righteous, and its

45
00:02:24,031 --> 00:02:25,831
fragrance shall be in their bones.

46
00:02:26,281 --> 00:02:29,411
The last book of every Bible
has a tree like this: the

47
00:02:29,411 --> 00:02:32,019
tree of life, for the
healing of the nations.

48
00:02:32,469 --> 00:02:34,982
But Enoch's road turned east, and the air

49
00:02:34,982 --> 00:02:36,821
changed. What did it smell of?

50
00:02:38,771 --> 00:02:42,846
Frankincense and myrrh. Then
mastic, cinnamon, nard and pepper.

51
00:02:43,296 --> 00:02:46,244
Then he passed above the
Erythraean Sea: the Greek

52
00:02:46,244 --> 00:02:48,779
name for the Red Sea
and the waters beyond.

53
00:02:49,229 --> 00:02:53,815
One scholar, J. T. Milik, tried to
map the plants to real spice lands.

54
00:02:54,265 --> 00:02:56,680
Another, Moshe Gil, said the scents point

55
00:02:56,680 --> 00:02:58,447
to eternal life, not to a map.

56
00:02:58,897 --> 00:03:02,673
Either way, the Erythraean Sea
was a real sea. Who sailed it?

57
00:03:04,623 --> 00:03:07,251
Did you know? A Greek
sailing guide from the

58
00:03:07,251 --> 00:03:09,700
first century is named for that same sea.

59
00:03:10,150 --> 00:03:13,703
It describes Adulis, the port
of Aksum, and a coast whose

60
00:03:13,703 --> 00:03:17,318
frankincense came in great
quantity and of the best grade.

61
00:03:17,768 --> 00:03:21,949
The incense on Enoch's road was
the trade of the Horn of Africa.

62
00:03:22,399 --> 00:03:25,466
Beyond the sea, Enoch found
a garden. In it stood

63
00:03:25,466 --> 00:03:28,095
the tree of wisdom. Who had eaten from it?

64
00:03:30,045 --> 00:03:32,962
Raphael said: your first
father and mother ate from

65
00:03:32,962 --> 00:03:35,421
it, and they were driven
out of the garden.

66
00:03:35,871 --> 00:03:38,325
At the ends of the earth,
Uriel showed him the

67
00:03:38,325 --> 00:03:40,565
gates of heaven, where the stars come out.

68
00:03:41,015 --> 00:03:43,912
And Enoch wrote down every
one: their number, their

69
00:03:43,912 --> 00:03:46,071
names, their courses and their months.

70
00:03:46,521 --> 00:03:48,441
So how did his writing reach us?

71
00:03:50,391 --> 00:03:53,089
Did you know? The oldest
known Ge'ez copy of

72
00:03:53,089 --> 00:03:55,297
Enoch was hidden under another book.

73
00:03:55,747 --> 00:03:59,443
In a Berlin library, a commentary
on Revelation from the

74
00:03:59,443 --> 00:04:02,809
sixteen hundreds had been
written over older pages.

75
00:04:03,259 --> 00:04:07,390
In 2016, scholars lit it with
special light, and found Enoch

76
00:04:07,390 --> 00:04:10,832
underneath, from the thirteen
hundreds or earlier.

77
00:04:12,782 --> 00:04:16,409
Online, Enoch gets sold as a
banned book of secret codes.

78
00:04:16,859 --> 00:04:21,049
We traced this one through a
1917 translation, Dead Sea

79
00:04:21,049 --> 00:04:25,392
fragments, a Greek sailing
guide and a Berlin manuscript.

80
00:04:25,842 --> 00:04:28,786
Before you share a claim,
ask: who wrote it, and when?

81
00:04:30,736 --> 00:04:34,363
An angel asked Enoch: why are
you so eager for the truth?

82
00:04:34,813 --> 00:04:37,495
Curiosity can turn into fear, or into the

83
00:04:37,495 --> 00:04:39,719
pride of knowing everything first.

84
00:04:40,169 --> 00:04:44,137
Enoch's answer, at every gate,
was to bless the Lord of Glory.

85
00:04:44,587 --> 00:04:48,193
Read a few verses slowly tonight,
and let wonder become prayer.

86
00:04:50,143 --> 00:04:52,233
Thank you for sitting with us over coffee.

87
00:04:52,683 --> 00:04:54,155
This is Ethiopics.
